const packages = [
  { id: 'trv', tier: 'Single valve', name: 'TRV supplied and fitted', price: '£65', unit: 'per radiator, inc VAT',
    points: ['New thermostatic valve and matching lockshield where needed', 'Drain down or freezing kit as needed', 'Refilled, bled and leak checked'] },
  { id: 'six-trvs', tier: 'Whole house', popular: true, name: 'Up to 6 TRVs supplied and fitted', price: '£295', unit: 'up to 6 radiators, inc VAT',
    points: ['Save £95 on six valves', 'One drain down for the whole job', 'Usually done in half a day'] },
  { id: 'leak', tier: 'Repair', name: 'Leaking radiator valve repair', price: '£120', unit: 'first hour, weekdays 9am–4pm, inc VAT',
    points: ['No call-out fee', 'Most valve leaks fixed in the first hour', '£150 evenings and weekends, £180 bank holidays'] },
  { id: 'pk-smart', tier: 'Smart heating', name: 'Fit your own smart radiator valves', price: '£65', unit: 'per radiator, inc VAT',
    points: ['Tado, Hive, Drayton Wiser, Netatmo, Danfoss and others', 'Fitted, paired and tested', 'Old manual valve heads taken off'] },
];

const faqs = [
  { q: 'How much does radiator valve replacement cost in Liverpool?', a: 'With us, a thermostatic radiator valve (TRV) supplied and fitted is £65 including VAT. Up to six TRVs are £295. A manual valve pair swap is also £65 per radiator. A leaking valve repair is charged at our first-hour rate of £120 on weekdays, with no call-out fee.' },
  { q: 'Do you have to drain the system to change a radiator valve?', a: 'Sometimes. On a sealed combi system we can often drain just enough water to get below the valve. On some jobs we use a freezing kit to freeze the pipe instead. For several valves at once, one full drain down is often quickest.' },
  { q: 'How long does it take to fit a TRV?', a: 'Most single TRVs take 30 minutes to an hour, including the refill and bleed. Six valves usually take about half a day.' },
  { q: 'What is the difference between a TRV and a lockshield valve?', a: 'The TRV is the one you turn. It senses the room and shuts off the hot water when the room is warm enough. The lockshield sits on the other end, under a plain cap. It is set once to balance the heat, then left alone.' },
  { q: 'Why does one radiator not have a TRV?', a: 'Water needs somewhere to go when every TRV has closed. So one radiator is usually left without a TRV, often in the hall. Your room thermostat is often in the same space. If your system has an automatic bypass valve, this matters less.' },
  { q: 'My radiator is cold but the others are hot. Is the TRV stuck?', a: 'Often, yes. TRV pins stick after summer. Take the head off, and gently push the pin in and out a few times. If it will not move, or the radiator is still cold, call us. It may need bleeding, balancing or a new valve.' },
  { q: 'Why is my radiator valve leaking?', a: 'The most common causes are a worn gland around the spindle, a loose nut on the pipe joint, or a worn valve tail. Some leaks just need tightening or a new seal. Others need a new valve. We find the cause and give you the price before we fit parts.' },
  { q: 'What should I do if a radiator valve is leaking now?', a: 'Put a bowl and towels under it. Close both valves on that radiator by turning them clockwise. If the leak will not stop, turn off the water at the stopcock and call 0151 558 0334.' },
  { q: 'Do TRVs save money?', a: 'They can help cut wasted heating. You can keep spare rooms cooler and heat the rooms you use. They work best with a room thermostat and a timer or smart thermostat.' },
  { q: 'Can you fit smart radiator valves I bought?', a: 'Yes. Fitting your own smart radiator valves is £65 per radiator. We fit Tado, Hive, Drayton Wiser, Netatmo, Danfoss and most other brands. Most smart heads screw onto a standard TRV body, sometimes with an adaptor that comes in the box.' },
  { q: 'Will a smart valve fit my old radiator valve?', a: 'Many will, with the right adaptor. If your valve is very old, worn or not compatible, we fit a new TRV body first. We tell you the price before we start.' },
  { q: 'Do I need to change both valves on a radiator?', a: 'Not always. If the lockshield is sound, we may keep it. Our £65 TRV price includes a matching lockshield where one is needed, so you are not caught out.' },
  { q: 'Will a new valve fix noisy or cold radiators?', a: 'It depends on the cause. A stuck or faulty valve, yes. But cold patches at the bottom usually mean sludge, which a power flush clears. Banging or gurgling often means air or low pressure. We check before we change anything.' },
  { q: 'Do you cover my area?', a: 'Yes. We cover all of Liverpool, plus the Wirral, Sefton, Knowsley and St Helens. Call 0151 558 0334 to check the next free slot.' },
];
